@startuml
title Edit Nail Art — blocked for clients (simple ↔ complex)

actor Client
participant "FE (Next.js client)" as FE
participant "NGINX" as NGINX
participant "BE (Django/DRF)" as BE

== Client-side guard (UX) ==
Client -> FE : tap "Alterar nail art" on a booked nail-art appointment
note over FE
  Modal (with close button) opens immediately:
  "Nail art changes (simple ↔ complex) are made by the
   esteticista — please talk to her directly."
  Clients can book nail art but never change it themselves
  (see business-rules.md). No API call needed for the UX.
end note
FE --> Client : informational modal

== Server-side enforcement (defense) ==
Client -> FE : (any client attempt to change nail art)
FE -> NGINX : POST /v1/appointments/{id}/nail-art/
NGINX -> BE : proxy
note over BE
  appointments.views.AppointmentNailArtBlockedView
  AuthZ: owner client; always raises PermissionDenied (403)
  Only staff edit Nail Art (BO — Phase 5.6).
end note
BE --> FE : 403 (staff-only change)
@enduml
